--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PROJECT DESCRIPTION & MISSION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BudgetBasics is an advanced, high-performance financial literacy and smart 
budgeting portal designed as a Single Page Application (SPA) to teach students, 
interns, and young professionals personal finance and budgeting fundamentals. 

The website features:
- Deep Dive educational breakdowns (Income & Inflows, Fixed vs Variable, Pay Yourself First).
- Interactive 50-30-20 & Custom Split Calculators with dynamic Range Sliders and Chart.js.
- S.M.A.R.T. Savings Goal Projections with Multi-Bucket CRUD and Timeline Accumulation Charts.
- Gamified Needs-vs-Wants interactive decision classifier.
- Personal Salary & Expense Budget Planner with full CRUD, Category Filters, and CSV Export.
- Smart Dynamic Financial Advisor analyzing safe spending limits and deficit recovery plans.
- 4-Pillar Financial Health Scorecard with printable verified Certificate of Achievement.
- Visual Infographics Gallery with Search, Sort, and Lightbox inspection modals.
- BeeBot AI offline financial assistant with client-side NLP pattern matching.
- Obsidian Black & Mint Green modern theme engine with instant light/dark toggle.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. MANDATORY INSTALLATION & EXECUTION INSTRUCTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 1: Extract the project archive or clone from GitHub.
Step 2: To run the project locally:

        Method A (Direct Browser Launch - Fastest):
        - Double-click index.html in any modern browser (Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Mozilla Firefox, Brave).

        Method B (Using Local Web Server - Recommended for JSON fetch):
        - Open Terminal / PowerShell in the project directory.
        - Run command: python -m http.server 8000
        - Open your browser and navigate to: http://localhost:8000

        Method C (Using VS Code Live Server):
        - Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
        - Right-click index.html and select "Open with Live Server".

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. MATHEMATICAL & CALCULATION FORMULAS USED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. 50-30-20 Allocation Formula:
   - Needs = Monthly Income * 50%
   - Wants = Monthly Income * 30%
   - Savings = Monthly Income * 20%
   (Also supports 60/20/20 Hostel Student and 40/20/40 Aggressive Saver models)

2. S.M.A.R.T. Savings Goal Calculations:
   - Remaining to Save = Target Amount - Current Savings
   - Funding Progress (%) = (Current Savings / Target Amount) * 100
   - Months to Reach Target = ceil(Remaining to Save / Monthly Contribution)
   - Weekly Saving Pace = Monthly Contribution / 4
   - Daily Saving Pace = Monthly Contribution / 30

3. Expense Planner Budget Variance:
   - Total Spent = Sum of all logged expense records
   - Remaining Budget = Monthly Salary - Total Spent
   - Spent Ratio (%) = (Total Spent / Monthly Salary) * 100
   - Needs Usage (%) = (Spent on Needs / Target Needs Budget) * 100
   - Wants Usage (%) = (Spent on Wants / Target Wants Budget) * 100
   - Daily Safe Wants Cap = (Remaining Wants) / 15 days

4. Financial Health Score Matrix (0 to 40 Points):
   - Pillar 1 (Savings Timing): Immediate Day 1 (10 pts) -> Month-end (2 pts)
   - Pillar 2 (Impulse Delay 24h): Consistent 24h delay (10 pts) -> Instant impulse (2 pts)
   - Pillar 3 (Expense Tracking): Daily detailed logging (10 pts) -> No tracking (2 pts)
   - Pillar 4 (Emergency Shield): 1-2 months cushion (10 pts) -> Zero cushion (0 pts)
   - Rating: 34-40 Master | 24-33 Disciplined | 14-23 Developing | <14 High Risk

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. LIST OF ASSUMPTIONS MADE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Assumption 1 (Zero-Backend Constraint):
The application adheres strictly to the Aptech SRS "No-Backend" constraint. 
All data persistence is handled via Client-Side LocalStorage, and pre-populated 
data is loaded from JSON files in the /data directory with offline fallbacks.

Assumption 2 (Multi-Currency Flexibility):
Currency values can be dynamically toggled across PKR, USD, INR, EUR, and GBP. 
Default currency is set to PKR (Rs 35,000 allowance benchmark).

Assumption 3 (Data Privacy & Validation):
Feedback and Contact forms perform client-side validation and render 
interactive toast confirmations without transmitting sensitive data to external servers.

Assumption 4 (Offline AI Assistant):
The AI Chatbot ("BeeBot AI") executes an in-browser NLP token matching 
engine against a structured JSON intent knowledge base, guaranteeing 100% 
offline availability without third-party API dependencies or cost.

